Allocate a video buffer in mgba-headless so rendering happens.

Without a video buffer the core skips rendering entirely (see the comment
in mGBA's src/platform/example/client-server/server.c), which makes the
Lua `emu:screenshot()` binding crash on a null pixel buffer. The GUI
frontends always attach one, so this only matters when running the
Goobster GBA harness against a headless dev build (e.g. CI or a server
with no display). Verified against mGBA master (0.11-dev, 2026-07).

Apply from the mGBA source root:
    patch -p1 < mgba-headless-videobuffer.patch

diff --git a/src/platform/headless-main.c b/src/platform/headless-main.c
index 61110b1..2d4e23a 100644
--- a/src/platform/headless-main.c
+++ b/src/platform/headless-main.c
@@ -165,6 +165,11 @@ int main(int argc, char * argv[]) {
 		goto loadError;
 	}
 
+	unsigned videoWidth, videoHeight;
+	core->baseVideoSize(core, &videoWidth, &videoHeight);
+	void* videoBuffer = malloc(videoWidth * videoHeight * BYTES_PER_PIXEL);
+	core->setVideoBuffer(core, videoBuffer, videoWidth);
+
 #ifdef ENABLE_DEBUGGERS
 	struct mDebugger debugger;
 	mDebuggerInit(&debugger);
